SUMMARY: The Tragically Hip - 10 Years Later - The Final Show
DESCRIPTION:Join us for yet another HISTORIC Tragically Hip evening - exa
 ctly 10 years later. Nearly 12 million watched 10 years ago\, and we will
  re-live that night again here in 2026.\n\n\nThis is a FREE event — reser
 ve your free tickets via the link right here.\n\n\nGRAND DOOR PRIZE (see 
 below):\n\nLive July 22 – August 20\, 2016\, a 3LP set commemorating the 
 best\, 29-track sampling of that tour’s expansive setlist PLUS Victrola R
 ETRO bluetooth record player - to go along with your new record set\n\n\n
 FREE • FREE • FREE • FREE\n\nWe’re dimming the lights and taking everyone
  back exactly 10 years…\n\nThe final 2016 live show from Kingston\, Ontar
 io — on the 8 big screens at Cat’s Cradle\, with big sound\, and dozens o
 f fellow Tragically Hip fans.\n\nThe final show on the tour was held on A
 ugust 20\, 2016 at the Rogers K-Rock Centre in the band's hometown of Kin
 gston. The concert was simulcast in a special\, The Tragically Hip: A Nat
 ional Celebration\, airing commercial-free across the CBC's television an
 d radio outlets\, including CBC Television\, CBC Radio One and CBC Radio 
 2\, as well as on Sirius XM satellite radio\, and online via CBC Music an
 d YouTube.\n\nCBC broke away from its second-last night of primetime cove
 rage of the 2016 Summer Olympics to air the concert\; Ron Maclean hosted 
 a short introduction from Rio de Janeiro\, where the Canadian Olympic ath
 letes were themselves gathered for a viewing party at Canada House. At th
 e end of the introduction\, Maclean said: "We now go to this late breakin
 g story on the CBC" referencing not only the concert itself but a lyric f
 rom the Tragically Hip song "Wheat Kings".\n\nAt least 11.7 million watch
 ed part of the concert across these platforms.\n\n\n*** please note this 
 is a spectacular audio/video tribute theme show\, with no artist particip
