SUMMARY: Frequency: Janel Jones + Atonal
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Frequency — a monthly live music series at Worth 
 Gallery. Curated by our Sound Director Janel Jones. Frequency spotlights 
 BIPOC musicians of varying genres through intimate\, stripped-back shows.
  Celebrating sound\, connection\, and creative expression in Toronto's vi
 brant music scene. Find your new favorite musician in your new favorite g
 allery. This month we welcome back Janel Jones\, who'll be crafting a spe
 cial night of visual and sonic soundscapes with Atonal. Janel is a multi-
 disciplinary artist and songwriter whose practice centers healing\, refle
 ction\, and play through sound. Rooted in jazz\, soul\, and contemporary 
 improvisation\, Janel's sound is shaped by their Carribean heritage and o
 ver a decade performing within Toronto's music community. Their music hon
 ors the ancestors\, and holds the complexities of their intersectional ea
 rth experience. Atonal is the solo project of Kalina Nedelcheva\, who ble
 nds experimental poetry\, improvisation\, and sound recording to create c
 ontemplative ecosystems that explore how sound affects our understanding 
 of images\, memories\, the environment\, and language.
CATEGORIES:Concert,Art-Show/Gallery-Event,Spoken-Word/Poetry,Worth-Galler
 y
