SUMMARY: Killer B Cinema Presents: Lady Battle Cop!
DESCRIPTION:On September 4th\, join us for the best Robocop knock-off you
  will see! Lady Battle Cop!\n\nAdvanced tickets are $5\; tickets at the d
 oor are $8 (Space is limited\, and tickets sell out fast)!\n\nTicket link
 :\n\nDoors open at 7:30 pm\, and the movie begins at 8:00.\n\nTicket link
 : https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/1997151828882?aff=oddtdtcreator https://www
 .eventbrite.ca/e/1997151828882?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\n*NO outside food or d
 rinks\; please buy food and drinks from the venue.\n\n\n*All films have c
 losed captioning.\n\n\nMovie info:\n\nTwo seemingly invincible fighters\,
  one good\, one evil\, square off in this sci-fi action opus from Japan. 
 When a four-man terrorist group known as Team Phantom begins raising havo
 c in downtown Tokyo\, the city is in desperate need of a hero. An unexpec
 ted champion emerges as Lady Battle Cop\, a former female tennis champion
  transformed into a seemingly unstoppable cyborg. That’s right. A female 
 Robocop!\n\nSome say this is a Japanese knockoff of Robocop\, and they wo
 uldn’t be wrong. We say it’s the best damn Robocop movie you will see!\n\
 n\nInfo about See-Scape:\n\nOur movies will be shown on the second floor!
  There are two bars available in See-Scape. The bar on the second floor i
 s open during our event and is cash-only. Debit/Credit purchases are avai
 lable on the main floor.\n\n\nSee-Scape also has an amazing menu. To lear
 n more about See-Scape\, please click here! www.seescapeto.com/ https://w
 ww.seescapeto.com/\n\n\nSee-Scape is located at 347 Keele Street (the clo
 sest intersection is Keele/Dundas) and is easily accessible via TTC. (fro
 m Keele Station or Dundas West Station)\n\n\nParking: There is a Green P 
 parking lot beside See-Scape and a few other paid parking lots nearby.\n\
 n\nEach month\, join Lizzie Violet & Zoltan Du Lac for killer B-moves fro
 m the 1930s to the present!\n\n\nPlease like our Facebook page and Instag
 ram @killerbcinema so you don’t miss an invite.\n\n\nThank you to See-Sca
 pe and their staff! They make our monthly event extra unforgettable!\n\n\
 nWe hope to see you at See-Scape.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Film,See-Scape
